The prompts and tool schemas in opencode.json, codex.json and qwen-code.json were
recorded from the requests those agents send. They keep their authors' licenses:

  opencode.json   OpenCode 1.19.5    https://github.com/sst/opencode       MIT (LICENSE-opencode-MIT.txt), Copyright (c) 2025 opencode
  codex.json      Codex CLI 0.166.0  https://github.com/openai/codex       Apache-2.0 (LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt), Copyright 2025 OpenAI
  qwen-code.json  Qwen Code 0.26.5   https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code   Apache-2.0 (LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt), Copyright 2025 Qwen Team

Changes made when recording: the working directory and home paths were replaced with
/home/dev/project and /home/dev, and the user's task with {task}. Codex CLI speaks the
Responses API; its request was converted to chat completions (developer messages merged
into one system message, namespaced tools flattened to ns__name, the hosted web_search
tool dropped).
